# villa_trim -- the roofline half of the villa's dress: the cornice that finishes every wall, the
# balustrade that turns the colonnade's top into a roof terrace, and the pantile course along the
# two side eaves where the hipped roof is seen end-on from the courtyard.
#
# Placed at the villa's own origin and yaw, so these are villa.part's local coordinates. The
# cornice and the balustrade are both 1 m kit runs, but only one of them may be stretched: a
# cornice's section is the same at every point along it, while a balustrade has balusters that
# would smear. So the cornices are single scaled pieces and the balustrade is twenty separate
# metres, cut to butt with no half-baluster at either end.

# cornice on the front colonnade's architrave (its face is at z -7.85) and on the other three walls
piece models/own/arch/cornice_run.obj    0.000  5.650  -7.850  21.000 1.000 1.000   0.0 0.0 0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/cornice_run.obj    0.000  5.650   7.850  21.000 1.000 1.000 180.0 0.0 0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/cornice_run.obj  -10.000  5.550   0.000  12.000 1.000 1.000  90.0 0.0 0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.8
piece models/own/arch/cornice_run.obj   10.000  5.550   0.000  12.000 1.000 1.000 270.0 0.0 0.0   1.67 1.73 1.83  tex plaster_smooth 0.8

